<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-dactylioceras-commune-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Dactylioceras commune Turing k_c at 24 µm (pass 2) (Dactylioceras commune (Sowerby, 1815), Toarcian, 181 Ma)",
        "Dactylioceras commune Turing k_c at 24 µm (pass 2) faithfully reproduces Dactylioceras commune (Sowerby, 1815), Toarcian, 181 Ma morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-dactylioceras-commune-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-dactylioceras-commune-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-dactylioceras-commune-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-dactylioceras-commune-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Dactylioceras commune (Sowerby, 1815), Toarcian, 181 Ma specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-dactylioceras-commune-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Dactylioceras commune (Sowerby, 1815), Toarcian, 181 Ma" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: 24 µm stripes are not resolved across the 57 mm photograph.",
        "does_not_claim: D_f = 1.55 was not measured on an exposed suture in this image.",
        "does_not_claim: No nanopublication was signed: ~/.nanopub/profile.yml is absent.",
        "does_not_claim: No second language model scored this audit.",
        "does_not_claim: The PDE did not generate the pyrite texture.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Accretion GIF whose last frame is the specimen, plus a 216 µm stripe patch where 24.19 µm is resolved.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Du = 5.789 and Dv = 41.680 µm² per time so the k_c formula returns 24.19 µm at ratio 7.2.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Eigenvector-seeded PDE growth rates versus analytical sigma(k).",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Outer-whorl rib harmonic 44 and spacing 3.484 mm from the photograph.",
        "reported_in_source: Catalogue: 181 Ma, 2.419e-05 m, D_f = 1.55, Ceratites 1.088 mm at 240 Ma, Placenticeras 2.53 mm at 75 Ma.",
        "reported_in_source: García-Ruiz, Checa and Rivas 1990 and Lutz and Boyajian 1995: ammonoid sutures are morphogenetic and fractal.",
        "reported_in_source: James St. John, CC BY 2.0: 57 mm Whitby Formation shell, Toarcian.",
        "reported_in_source: Meinhardt and Klingler 1987 and Fowler, Meinhardt and Prusinkiewicz 1992: pigment laid down at a molluscan aperture.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 critical wavenumber and Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics.",
        "transfer_boundary: Aperture pigment reaction-diffusion is transferred to a 24 µm periostracal patch of an ammonite. The whole-shell pixels are the fossil, not a PDE solution.",
        "transfer_boundary: Neighbor organ-scale wavelengths are the intervals tiled by this detail wave. Their diffusion coefficients are not reused." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Dactylioceras commune (Early Jurassic (Toarcian, 181 Ma))" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Ostrakoderma (Mollusca & Echinodermata)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Dactylioceras" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-dactylioceras-commune-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/dactylioceras_commune_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Dactylioceras commune (Sowerby, 1815), Toarcian, 181 Ma; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952 critical wavenumber and Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics. | Meinhardt and Klingler 1987 and Fowler, Meinhardt and Prusinkiewicz 1992: pigment laid down at a molluscan aperture. | García-Ruiz, Checa and Rivas 1990 and Lutz and Boyajian 1995: ammonoid sutures are morphogenetic and fractal. | James St. John, CC BY 2.0: 57 mm Whitby Formation shell, Toarcian. | Catalogue: 181 Ma, 2.419e-05 m, D_f = 1.55, Ceratites 1.088 mm at 240 Ma, Placenticeras 2.53 mm at 75 Ma.; reconstructed_in_script: Du = 5.789 and Dv = 41.680 µm² per time so the k_c formula returns 24.19 µm at ratio 7.2. | Eigenvector-seeded PDE growth rates versus analytical sigma(k). | Outer-whorl rib harmonic 44 and spacing 3.484 mm from the photograph. | Accretion GIF whose last frame is the specimen, plus a 216 µm stripe patch where 24.19 µm is resolved.; transfer_boundary: Aperture pigment reaction-diffusion is transferred to a 24 µm periostracal patch of an ammonite. The whole-shell pixels are the fossil, not a PDE solution. | Neighbor organ-scale wavelengths are the intervals tiled by this detail wave. Their diffusion coefficients are not reused.; does_not_claim: 24 µm stripes are not resolved across the 57 mm photograph. | D_f = 1.55 was not measured on an exposed suture in this image. | The PDE did not generate the pyrite texture. | No nanopublication was signed: ~/.nanopub/profile.yml is absent. | No second language model scored this audit.]; other sources: Dactylioceras commune ammonite fossil from Yorkshire, England <https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dactylioceras_commune_Ammonite_Fossil_from_Yorkshire_England.jpg>; phenomenon_size: 30 µm (2.99e-05 m, log10=-4.524 m, tier=4_cellular_10um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 30 µm to 6.7 cm): 30 µm:dactylioceras-commune-bioelectric-polarity, 93 µm:dactylioceras-commune-vertex-packing, 1.5 mm:dactylioceras-commune-turing-wavelength, 3.0 mm:dactylioceras-commune-clock-wavefront, 6.7 mm:dactylioceras-commune-morphogen-condensation, 8.2 mm:dactylioceras-commune-elastic-buckling, 9.3 mm:dactylioceras-commune-flux-canalization, 1.3 cm:dactylioceras-commune-branching-tree" ;
